      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-17839",
      ":question/problem": "The graph of $y = f(-x) - 3$ can be obtained from the graph of $y = f(x)$ by applying **some** of the following transformations:\n\n- $(T1)$ - Reflection across the $x$-axis\n- $(T2)$ - Stretch of scale factor $3$ parallel to the $y$-axis\n- $(T3)$ - Translation by $3$ units down\n- $(T4)$ - Reflection across the $y$-axis\n\nWhich of the following could be a possible ordering of the appropriate transformations?"
